hHQk", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20298, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_019Vt9D7FisvExGvuW1TiDiL", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20598, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_019Vt9D7FisvExGvuW1TiDiL", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20598, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019Vt9D7FisvExGvuW1TiDiL", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24930, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DVtM4Jupwcc7dqS8WxpU4x", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and has been failing health checks since, with an error rate of 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, investigate the orchestrator error during the rollback, and find out why a build that was unhealthy in staging was promoted to production."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55530, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DVtM4Jupwcc7dqS8WxpU4x", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55530, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DVtM4Jupwcc7dqS8WxpU4x", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57751, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WhZLUMfu79vvznt7rUv3mQ", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58051, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WhZLUMfu79vvznt7rUv3mQ", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58051, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WhZLUMfu79vvznt7rUv3mQ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63397, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. Since it had been healthy before, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left the regions on mixed versions: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. I tried again and the second attempt finished.\n- Now all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate page.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the halted first attempt) and the current state. It also lists three follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate had already failed health checks in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015k8uPkP6UMMvRVYfSb7Ydx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BsgpcDUVWeqm1uBSfXRhh2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AXdvcrbt8WdcuK14q5zLVA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LfT6TuG4eFr7RwmDHVoYux", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a healthy version doesn't need approval, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SmzpWocNbfYHs9owCaXmDa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015hHypdiCbGoKkppecRhHQk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019Vt9D7FisvExGvuW1TiDiL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DVtM4Jupwcc7dqS8WxpU4x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and has been failing health checks since, with an error rate of 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A retry finished the rollback. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, investigate the orchestrator error during the rollback, and find out why a build that was unhealthy in staging was promoted to production."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may still have been created. I'll check before retrying so the on-call engineer doesn't get paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WhZLUMfu79vvznt7rUv3mQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n**Rollback**\n- v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. v2.3.0 was the most recent release that had been healthy in production. Since it had been healthy before, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error. That left the regions on mixed versions: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. I tried again and the second attempt finished.\n- Now all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate page.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the halted first attempt) and the current state. It also lists three follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error, and find out why v2.3.1 reached production when its release candidate had already failed health checks in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}